# Check text files out with LF on every machine, overriding Git for Windows' system-wide
# core.autocrlf=true. Bash scripts (WSLSetup.sh, .githooks/pre-commit) break with CRLF, and most apps behind
# the symlinked configs (Windows Terminal, VS Code) save LF anyway, which made git warn "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" on every status. Some save CRLF (UniGetUI, PowerToys' FancyZones): git stores those as LF and warns
# "CRLF will be replaced by LF" until the next checkout - harmless.
* text=auto eol=lf
